+    "_why_r7b": "r7b (27 Oct): the Meshy albedos carry almost no window texels, so the thresholded masks (0.5%) lit only specks. Authored warm window-grid masks on the stone-wall texels (keep 2.1%, spire 3.2%; the old masks unioned in), energy 7/12 -> 5/6. CPU judged against shipping in one batch with r7 and r6b (three fresh code-blind judges, JUDGE_PROMPT verbatim, 3 anchor pairs incl. craft; calibrate.py linear slope 1.38, r 0.99, RMSE 0.14; band5_stronghold_approach_0 day/night; ralph/reports/MEADOWS/close-1024/r7-1027-mapped.json): shipping 6.00 -> r6b 6.27, r7 6.50, r7b 6.69 (+0.69). Judges 3/3: the lit-window castle is the best night landmark of the three. Open: the windows tonemap white rather than warm and glow by day too; the keep floats over the canopy with no visible base; the night grade crushes the grove. CPU no longer closes a row: OFF until the GPU pass.", "_why_r7": "r7 (OFF; coordinator ask after the r6b CPU judges, 3/3: a lone tower, not fortress mass, and no windows reading at night): the r5 lit keep returns as the main piece for mass and warm windows (width_m 120, about 134 m tall; emission 2.5 -> 7), and the r6b spire stands 70 m behind it and 22 m to one side as a `companions` entry (stronghold_hero_gatehouse.gd second hero slot; about 200 m tall, emission 8 -> 12), so the skyline reads as one keep with a tower rising above it.", "_why_r6b_cpu": "r6b CPU judged (27 Oct; three fresh code-blind judges, JUDGE_PROMPT verbatim, 3 anchor pairs incl. craft, linear slope 1.40, r 0.92, RMSE 0.31; band5_stronghold_approach_0 day/night approach and gameplay; ralph/reports/MEADOWS/close-1024/spire1027-mapped.json): shipping 5.5/4.8/5.3 vs 6.0/5.4/5.9, mapped 4.93 -> 5.72 (+0.79); P2-003 PRESENT -> PARTIAL 3/3 (the first landmark read from these woods). Open (3/3): a thin lone tower, not fortress mass (walls, keep body); no warm windows reading at night; out of the gameplay view. CPU no longer closes a row: OFF until the GPU pass.", "_why_r6b": "r6b: the first CPU frame at band5_stronghold_approach_0 (about 440 m out) showed the 120 m spire as a thin pale sliver behind the trees, and its windows did not read at night. width_m 27.4 -> 45.7 (about 200 m tall) and emission_energy 4 -> 8.",
